- [x] `src/cli/init/.aide` outcomes.desired ("The `obsidian` MCP server entry is always written into `.mcp.json` by the CLI..."): the entire bullet repeats the wrong key shape — "obsidian MCP server entry" should read "brain MCP server entry" (with the entry value carrying an obsidian-shaped command/args that the registry will identify as the `obsidian` driver).
  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled) — fixed `brain` MCP key.
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/cli/init/.aide` outcomes.undesired ("The CLI fails to write the `obsidian` MCP server entry on a run where `--vault-path` was not supplied..."): same key-name drift. The undesired outcome is structurally still load-bearing (the entry must always be written) but the key it names is stale.
  Traces to: `.aide/handoff.aide` (settled).
